@.str.64 = private unnamed_addr constant [1284 x i8] c"The general entrance for reading a TriangleMesh from a file.\0AThe function calls read functions based on the extension name of filename.\0ASupported formats are `obj, ply, stl, off, gltf, glb, fbx`.\0A\0AThe following example reads a triangle mesh with the .ply extension::\0A    import open3d as o3d\0A    mesh = o3d.t.io.read_triangle_mesh('mesh.ply')\0A\0AArgs:\0A    filename (str): Path to the mesh file.\0A    enable_post_processing (bool): If True enables post-processing.\0A        Post-processing will\0A          - triangulate meshes with polygonal faces\0A          - remove redundant materials\0A          - pretransform vertices\0A          - generate face normals if needed\0A\0A        For more information see ASSIMPs documentation on the flags\0A        `aiProcessPreset_TargetRealtime_Fast, aiProcess_RemoveRedundantMaterials,\0A        aiProcess_OptimizeMeshes, aiProcess_PreTransformVertices`.\0A\0A        Note that identical vertices will always be joined regardless of whether\0A        post-processing is enabled or not, which changes the number of vertices\0A        in the mesh.\0A\0A        The `ply`-format is not affected by the post-processing.\0A\0A    print_progress (bool): If True print the reading progress to the terminal.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    Returns the mesh object. On failure an empty mesh is returned.\0A\00", align 1
